  "interpretation": "The shared I-JEPA encoder ends with substantial CLS-like information in visual tokens: the control has 0.5623 CLS-patch alignment and 0.4436 within-image patch cosine. Separate normalization, LayerScale, and early QKV paths reduce those values to -0.0025 and 0.3442 while preserving spatial energy and improving the online peak by 0.32 percentage points. This is a real routing effect, visible from block 1, but dense semantic utility is mixed through the middle blocks and the final patch-mean gain is only 0.62 percentage points. The tested separation is therefore useful architectural evidence, not a promoted I-JEPA replacement.",
